# Migration-narrowing gate allowlist.
#
# Format: CHECK_A|<rust_file>|<NAME>|<python_file>  # reason: <why this
# is a coincidental name collision, not a real capability narrowing>
#
# Every entry MUST carry a written reason and MUST be a coincidental
# name/identifier collision, not a real defect. Do NOT allowlist a genuine
# capability-narrowing defect (a Rust port silently dropping a
# parameter/precision the Python had) — that is the exact defect class this
# gate exists to catch. See scripts/check_migration_narrowing.py module
# docstring for the two seeded historical instances (H_CONV_BACKGROUND,
# escape_via.rs rotation).
#
# Seeded 2026-08-07 from a real `--init` run against origin/main
# (63ec4e756). At seed time this run additionally surfaced two more, not
# previously catalogued, live instances of the same defect class
# (net_ordering.rs `rotation` and terminal_planning.rs `initial_rotation`,
# both `Option<i64>` mirroring `float(comp.initial_rotation) * math.pi / 2.0`
# in obstacle_map.py) — those are intentionally NOT listed below; they are
# real findings, not false positives, and should stay failing until fixed.

# --- CHECK A: net_classification.py pattern-set constants ------------------
# These frozensets (GROUND_NET_PATTERNS, POWER_NET_PATTERNS, etc.) are NOT
# runtime parameters threaded into a Rust call — the Rust classifiers
# (`_rs.is_ground_net(name)` etc.) take only `name` and hard-code the same
# literal pattern sets internally. The Python constants exist so
# `tests/wave4_phase2/test_core_contracts_differential.py` can cross-check
# `oracle.GROUND_NET_PATTERNS` (etc.) against the Rust predicates'
# behaviour independently — i.e. there IS a differential guard here, just
# not a call-site argument. Confirmed by reading net_classification.py and
# its differential test; no call site exists where these could be threaded
# through as an argument in the first place.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|GROUND_NET_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: pattern-set constant hard-coded identically in the Rust classifier, not a threadable per-call parameter; cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|POWER_NET_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|HV_NET_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|GROUND_PIN_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|POWER_PIN_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|HV_PIN_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|CLOCK_PIN_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.

# --- CHECK B: short/common identifier collisions ----------------------------
# The four `v`/`i` entries that used to live here (pyo3_bridge.rs x2,
# deterministic_leaves.rs, req_safe_01.rs) are GONE, not moved: every one of
# them gave "coincidental identifier collision" as its own reason, and
# `MIN_CHECK_B_NAME_LEN` in scripts/check_migration_narrowing.py now
# generalizes that judgement instead of restating it once per pair. A binding
# shorter than 3 characters carries no cross-language identity, so Check B no
# longer emits those pairings at all and the entries went stale.
#
# `name` below survives the guard (4 characters) and is a genuinely different
# failure -- a regex over-match on dict-literal syntax, not a short-name
# collision -- so it still needs an explicit entry.
CHECK_B|packages/temper-design-bundle/src/pcl_parse.rs|name|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/metrics/physics.py  # reason: Rust `name` is a local match-arm binding for tier-int-to-string mapping (parse_tier) with no relation to geometry; Python match is a dict-literal `z.name: tuple(float(v) ...)` in physics.py:144, which the annotation-regex over-matches (dict-literal `key: value` syntax reads like a type annotation to the heuristic). Coincidental identifier collision + known regex limitation.
